      "op": "note",
      "text": "HALL-FX BUG-13/26a/67/71 flicker on a frozen clock: 10 s sequences of the office and the city view at the forced hours 9 (H1), 12 (H2), 16.75 (H3), 17 and 22 (H5) at A1 and A2, and at H2 and H5 at A3 and A4. Every hour here is forced (the cheat's DevToolsState.ForcedHour), so the lit share is constant in each sequence: these show that nothing toggles while the clock holds. Windows fading in on a running clock are hall_fx_dusk's (with HallFxRig). Pass: seqtools flicker on every sequence (no pixel toggling more than twice in 10 s outside the 8 tracked cars), plus the traffic tint (region_luma --track car0,...,car7 --stat p90, see docs/pending/HALL-FX.md). LIGHT's dust is hidden for the run ('Hall FX: dust', toggled back at the end): its shimmer is LIGHT's to measure (BUG-13 split, #11)."
